Z||000004||Fformula88||09-19-2001||10:35 AM||||I dunno about you guys, but I don't think I would want it as a state, or even as anything.  To permanently hold, or even occupy for a long time a country like AFghanistan would cost a lot of American lives... much more than it would be worth.<P>Sure I am for getting rid of the terrorists, but those people do not give up the fight.  remember the Soviet Union's 8 year occupation?  They finally pulled out because they simply could not pacify the country and got tired of seeing body bags full of their own young men piling up.  <P>Being a state would be worse yet!  You would be putting 2 senators, and countless representatives (there are 25 million people in Afghanistan) into our congress.  Sorry, but I do not want those fundamentalist freaks deciding on our countries policies.<P>Would you have us walk into Ireland and take it too since they run terrorist acts on Britain?  Britain is an ally we have sworn to protect.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
